  "description": "Implements Ethereum logs bloom filter functions: add_to_bloom and logs_bloom for the Osaka fork.",
  "sub_graphs": [
    {
      "id": "SG-osaka-bloom-module",
      "name": "Module Overview and Imports",
      "description": "Ethereum Logs Bloom module for the Osaka fork. Defines functions for calculating bloom filters of logs, which allow efficient searching of logs by address and/or topic by rapidly eliminating blocks and receipts from search. Bloom filters are 256-byte (2048-bit) bitfields where entries are hashed via keccak256 and 3 bits are set per entry.",
      "invariants": [
        {
          "id": "INV-osaka-bloom-001",
          "text": "A Bloom filter is always exactly 256 bytes (2048 bits) in size."
        },
